title: Presidential Election campaigning
subtitle: It's campaign season.
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.presidential_election_campaigning_seen = 1;
Q.dufour_funds = 0;
Q.dufour_support = 0;
if (Q.royalist_candidate_1932 == "Gallax") {
    Q.commons_royalist += 3;
    Q.burgher_royalist += 4;
    Q.guild_royalist += 4;
    Q.faithful_royalist += 2;
    Q.landed_royalist += 4;
    Q.disfavored_royalist += 4;
    Q.burgher_traditionalist -= 2;
    Q.guild_traditionalist -= 2; 
    Q.disfavored_collectivist -= 2;
} else if (Q.royalist_candidate_1932 == "Gorrick") {
    Q.guild_royalist += 4;
    Q.guild_traditionalist -= 4;
    Q.landed_royalist += 2;
    Q.landed_traditionalist -= 2;
    Q.commons_collectivist += 3;
    Q.commons_royalist -= 3;
}
!}
tags: event
view-if: year = 1932 and month >= 2 and not dufour_term_extended and not marcher_abstain_1932 and dufour_run
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/campaign.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
priority: -1
max-visits: 1
go-to: candidate_selection


= Presidential Election campaigning

[? if royalist_candidate_1932: The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, standing alone in the electoral fight to elect [+ royalist_candidate_1932_disp +], has little chance of winning—at least according to our advisors. However, this does not mean the election is inconsequential. The extensive <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> propaganda campaign, orchestrated by the infamous Joseph Goebbels, combined with the upcoming local elections just a month after the first round, could significantly shift public opinion. This, in turn, may pressure President DuFour and his entourage to adopt a more antagonistic stance toward the current government and push for a reorganization of the national government to include the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span>. [? if royalist_candidate_1932 == "Gallax": Furthermore, Adolf Gallax possesses a remarkable charismatic ability, and his strategy of flying across the Commonwealth to deliver speeches to hundreds of thousands of otherwise indifferent voters each day rivals even that of DuFour. ?][? if royalist_candidate_1932 == "Gorrick": With Gallax ineligible, Hermann Gorrick has taken up the mantle as the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>'s candidate. As aw staunch figure of the party’s right wing and an opponent of Crowde’s more radical policies, Gorrick will find it easier to attract industrial support, securing crucial funding for their extensive propaganda network. ?] ?]

[? if marcher_support_reactionary: With our support for President DuFour, we are excluded from the United DuFour Committees, the main organization promoting his candidacy. Our support is unwelcome by DuFour himself, while Westmore and Gereke, the key leaders of the United DuFour Committees, will attempt to distance themselves from us as much as possible to secure moderate right-wing and industrial backing. As a result, our role in the campaign will be to rally the Commonwealth Left, who remain reluctant to vote for a reactionary like him. ?][? if braun_campaign: We are running Otto Bristol, one of our most renowned and respected statesmen. His reformist stance has given us a chance to attract some crossover support from the bourgeois parties. However, many outside our party would sooner die than support a <span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span>. Our only viable path to expanding our vote share lies in winning back disaffected <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> and mobilizing worker enthusiasm. ?][? if marcher_support_thalmann: Our controversial decision to support [+ communist_candidate_1932_disp +] as a leftist unity candidate has deeply polarized Commonwealth politics, setting the stage for a final showdown between <span style="color: #9B0000;">Marxist</span> and Capitalism. A civil war is not even out of the question, regardless of which candidate emerges victorious. With the Commonwealth Left united behind [+ communist_candidate_1932 +], our electoral base has little room to grow—we can only hope that the workers turn out in full force at the polls. ?][? if rosenfeld_campaign: We are running Kurt Pendrigon, a lesser-known figure from our left wing. His leftist stances have given us a chance to attract the support of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span>, but have completely closed the door to support from the bourgeois parties. Our only viable path to expanding our vote share lies in winning back disaffected workers, mobilizing their enthusiasm, and persuading our more reformist middle-class and rural elements to stick with the plan. ?][? if eckener_campaign: We are running Hugo Eckhart, a famed non-partisan Zeppelin captain and personally conservative figure. His rightist stances have left the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> vulnerable to defections to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span>, but have completely opened the door to unified support from the bourgeois parties. We can either shore up support for Eckhart within the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> itself, or focus on maximizing crossover support and strengthening our cooperation with bourgeois allies. ?]

@candidate_selection

- @view_candidates: View the running candidates.

