We have lost an alarming number of voters to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> due to our support for the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> President DuFour. To ensure DuFour secures an outright majority in the first round, we must prevent further defections.

@bourgeois_campaign
on-arrival: {!
Q.dufour_unity = 10;
if (Q.dufour_angry_bruning >= 75) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.gold_defect) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.cnblp_defect) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.second_bruning_cabinet_seen) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.marcher_support_reactionary) Q.dufour_unity -= 3;
if (Q.royalist_votes >= 20) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.royalist_votes >= 30) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.royalist_votes >= 35) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.marcher_campaign || Q.marcher_support_thalmann || Q.collectivist_support_marcher) Q.dufour_unity += 3;
!}
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu

The United DuFour Committees have set to work improving the perception of moderate right-wing Commonwealth voters toward President DuFour, whose reputation as the Hero of Tannenberg has been tarnished by his support for the hated Unity system. Despite this, the <span class="tooltip-text" title="Following DuFour's overseeing of the Commonwealth's crushing victory at Tannenberg in the Great War, DuFour has become the center of a massive personality cult, lauded as the living ideal of Commonwealth masculinity and patriotism. He is the embodiment of the best virtues of Heartland tradition.">DuFour Mythos</span> remains intact[? if royalist_candidate_1932 == "Gallax":, and may be the only thing that rivals Gallax's charisma?].

It's their turn to campaign.

DuFour camp unity level: [+ dufour_unity : dufour_unity +]

@bourgeois_campaign_menu
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.unionist_support_marcher != 1) Q.religion_available = 1;
!}

- @eckener
- @industrial
- @religion
- @westarp
- @organizational_endorsements

@eckener
title: Famed Zeppelin Captain Hugo Eckhart is recruited for the campaign.
subtitle: Being a stanch support of the President, he will utilize the *Graf Zeppelin* for the campaign.
on-arrival: eckener_used = 1
max-visits: 1
go-to: eckener_2 if dufour_unity >= 8; eckener_3 if dufour_unity < 8

@eckener_2
on-arrival: dufour_support += 2
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu

In an attempt to rival the <span class="tooltip-text" title="good mod">dynamism</span> of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> campaign, which has utilized aircraft to quickly transport high-profile <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> leaders to deliver up to four speeches per day, Hugo Eckhart has been convinced to take flight across the Commonwealth to drum up popular support for DuFour. 

@eckener_3
on-arrival: disfavored_royalist += 6; disfavored_collectivist -= 3; disfavored_marcher -= 3
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu

In an attempt to rival the dynamism of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> campaign, the DuFour campaign initially tried to convince Graf Zeppelin pilot Hugo Eckhart to fly across the Commonwealth in support of DuFour. However, with Eckhart already scheduled for a flight to South America, the campaign had to pivot to an alternative approach. They opted to rent airplanes to drop twenty million leaflets over the Commonwealth population. However, this isn't enough to counteract the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> style of campaigning.

@industrial
title: Carl Duisberg of IG Farben will attempt to gain support of key industrialists.
subtitle: DuFour has lost the favor of many of his former backers, maybe they can be convinced again?
on-arrival: industry_used = 1
max-visits: 1
go-to: industrial_2 if dufour_unity >= 5; industrial_3 if dufour_unity < 5

Carl Duisberg, the chairman of the United DuFour Committees have largely been unsuccessful in convincing big business leaders to sign the petition for DuFour's reelection, but perhaps the gravity of this race would help convince them?

@industrial_2
on-arrival: dufour_support += 2
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu

Duisberg, being the former chairman of the National Federation of Commonwealth Industry (RDI) and one of the more moderate members, has been successful in soliciting donations from many business leaders who had reservations about backing DuFour again. The radical revolutionary and socialistic policies of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> have greatly discouraged them from donating to [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]. It now looks like the DuFour campaign finally has the resources to properly establish a campaign infrastructure that can rival Goebbels' efforts and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>.

@industrial_3
on-arrival: guild_royalist += 4; guild_kvp -= 2; guild_traditionalist -= 2 if industrial_traditionalist_backing >= 2 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_other -= 4; landed_royalist += 2
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu

Despite the antipathy the industrialists have toward [? if not gallax_deported: Gallax and the ?]<span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> due to their crypto-<span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> policies, a large part of them are firmly opposed to DuFour, and will withhold their donations. The DuFour campaign is beginning to heavily fall behind the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> in more rural areas, primarily due to the lack of resources.

@religion
title: The Catholic Church and Lutheran Church have long held political neutrality, perhaps that will change?
view-if: unionist_support_marcher != 1
on-arrival: religion_used = 1; faithful_unionist += 4 if faithful_unionist_normalized < 50; faithful_royalist -= 4 if faithful_unionist_normalized < 50 and faithful_royalist_normalized >= 8;
max-visits: 1
go-to: religion_2 if dufour_unity >= 3; religion_3 if dufour_unity < 3

Prominent leaders of the Lutheran Church have endorsed President DuFour, arguing that despite their historical political neutrality, his reelection is a pressing necessity. Meanwhile, the Catholic Church is even more united in support of DuFour than it was for Wilhelm Marx in 1925. Catholic leaders, historically skeptical of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazism</span>, have actively discouraged their members from joining <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> paramilitary organizations. This, combined with the strong support of Catholic-affiliated trade unions, will prove enormously significant in rallying a skeptical Catholic population behind a candidate whom most instinctively associate with Lutheran orthodoxy and Heartland authoritarianism.

@religion_2
on-arrival: dufour_support += 1
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu

Despite strong opposition from state and local Protestant church organizations—many of whose members sympathize with [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +] and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>—they have taken a public stand and will be campaigning in favor of DuFour, even amid growing calls for them to withdraw their endorsements.

@religion_3
on-arrival: burgher_royalist += 2; guild_royalist += 2; landed_royalist += 2; burgher_kvp -= 2; guild_kvp -= 2; landed_kvp -= 2; burgher_traditionalist -= 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_traditionalist -= 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; landed_traditionalist -= 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; burgher_other -= 2 if not kvp_formed; guild_other -= 2 if not kvp_formed; landed_other -= 2 if not kvp_formed
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu

Unfortunately for the DuFour campaign, the pro-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> sentiment within state and local churches has prevented church leaders from taking a public stand for DuFour. Many devout Protestants will now be voting for [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +] as a result, as the church now claims that intervening in a presidential election would be against its nature.

@westarp
title: Westmore, one of DuFour's close friends, will attempt to rally conservative forces for DuFour.
on-arrival: westarp_used = 1; dufour_support += 1
view-if: not marcher_campaign_1932
max-visits: 1
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu

Of course, the main goal of the United DuFour Committees is to dispel the notion that DuFour is supported by the <span style="color: #000000;">Black</span>-<span style="color: #c00000;">Red</span> parties. To this end, Westmore has sent a letter to 750 conservative elites who supported DuFour's election in 1925, with 500 reaffirming their support of DuFour today. [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": He has also played a key role in rallying the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> around his candidacy. ?]

@organizational_endorsements
title: What about the endorsements of the non-partisan organizations?
subtitle: Influential groups such as the RLB, DHV, and the Pan-Germans, have been growing a rift between themselves and DuFour.
view-if: eckener_used and industry_used and (religion_used or not religion_available) and (westarp_used or marcher_candidate_1932)
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.dufour_support) {
    Q.burgher_kvp += Q.dufour_support;
    Q.guild_kvp += Q.dufour_support; 
    Q.landed_kvp += Q.dufour_support;
    if (Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") {
        Q.burgher_traditionalist += Q.dufour_support;
        Q.guild_traditionalist += Q.dufour_support;
        Q.landed_traditionalist += Q.dufour_support;
    }
    Q.burgher_ddp += Q.dufour_support / 3; 
    Q.guild_ddp += Q.dufour_support / 3;
    Q.burgher_other += Q.dufour_support / 1.5;
    Q.guild_other += Q.dufour_support / 1.5;
    Q.burgher_gold += Q.dufour_support / 3;
    Q.guild_gold += Q.dufour_support / 3;
    Q.landed_other += Q.dufour_support / 1.5;
    Q.pro_republic += Q.dufour_support; 
    if (!Q.kvp_formed) Q.landed_other += Q.dufour_support;
    Q.burgher_royalist -= (Q.dufour_support*Q.royalist_votes) / 50;
    Q.old_royalist -= (Q.dufour_support*Q.royalist_votes) / 50;
    Q.landed_royalist -= (Q.dufour_support*Q.royalist_votes) / 50;
}
if (Q.rlb_royalist) {
    Q.rlb_dufour = 0;
    Q.landed_royalist += Q.landed_other*0.1;
    Q.landed_other *= 0.9;
    Q.landed_traditionalist *= 0.9;
} else if (!Q.rlb_royalist) {
    Q.rlb_dufour = 1;
    Q.landed_other += 4;
    if (Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") {
        Q.landed_traditionalist += 2;
    } else {
        Q.landed_kvp += 2;
    }
}
!}

National Rural League (RLB) - [? if rlb_dufour: <span style="color: #808080;">**[+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +]**</span> ?][? if not rlb_dufour: <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**[+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>[? if traditionalist_candidate_1932:&nbsp;or [? if traditionalist_candidate_1932 != "Mallin" or traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**[+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>?][? if traditionalist_candidate_1932 == "Mallin" and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**[+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>?]?] ?]

Wardens - [? if traditionalist_candidate_1932 and traditionalist_candidate_1932 != "Mallin":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**[+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>?][? if not traditionalist_candidate_1932 or traditionalist_candidate_1932 == "Mallin": <span style="color: #808080;">**[+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +]**</span> ?]

Commonwealth National Association of Commercial Employees (DHV) - <span style="color: #808080;">**[+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +]**</span>

Pan-Commonwealth League (ADV) - <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**[+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>[? if traditionalist_candidate_1932:&nbsp;or [? if traditionalist_candidate_1932 != "Mallin" or traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**[+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>?][? if traditionalist_candidate_1932 == "Mallin" and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**[+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>?]?]

United Patriotic Leagues (VVVD) - <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**[+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>[? if traditionalist_candidate_1932:&nbsp;or [? if traditionalist_candidate_1932 != "Mallin" or traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**[+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>?][? if traditionalist_candidate_1932 == "Mallin" and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**[+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>?]?]

Kyffhäuser League - <span style="color: #808080;">**[+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +]**</span>

[? if not rlb_royalist: Out of all the various right-wing interest organizations, the endorsement of the Commonwealth's largest economic interest group, the RLB, with its million members and numerous influential state organizations, is undoubtedly the most significant. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> strategy toward these organizations is not to attack them directly but to influence their rank-and-file members. This pressure forces leadership to either support the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> or risk discrediting themselves in the eyes of their members.<br><br> However, this approach has failed with the RLB. Under Schiele's leadership, the organization remains skeptical of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span> and has successfully blocked a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> appointee from joining the presidium. Despite this, strong <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> sympathies among the rank-and-file have led to defections to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span>'s alternative organization. ?]

[? if rlb_royalist: Out of all the various right-wing interest organizations, the endorsement of the Commonwealth's largest economic interest group, the RLB, with its million members and numerous influential state organizations, is undoubtedly the most significant. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> strategy toward these organizations is not to attack them directly but to influence their rank-and-file members. This pressure forces leadership to either support the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> or risk discrediting themselves in the eyes of their members. <br><br> This approach has proven successful within the RLB, as its new leader, Kalckreuth, is notably friendly toward the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span>. He has even appointed a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> agricultural official to the presidium. However, this shift has sparked significant backlash from the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>-aligned factions within the organization and from state affiliates in Avriza, Stathmore, and Purl. These groups have rejected the RLB's endorsement and instead urged their members to vote for [+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +][? if traditionalist_candidate_1932:&nbsp;or [+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +]?].?]

- @hope: Let's hope the Commonwealth will make the correct choice.

@campaigning_thalmann
view-if: marcher_support_thalmann

We have a plethora of campaign options at our disposal.

- @paramilitary
- @media_communist
- @united_left
- @campaigning
- @campaigning_hindenburg_op: It's DuFour's turn to campaign.

@paramilitary
title: Ally with the <span style="color: #700000;">Communist</span> <span style="color: #700000;">**RFB**</span> on the streets, to fight against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>.
subtitle: This will permanently alienate the bourgeois parties!
on-arrival: collectivist_truce = 1; collectivist_relation += 5; vanguard_strength += 100; banner_strength += 100; vanguard_militancy += 0.1; banner_militancy += 0.04; knight_dissent += 10; reformist_dissent += 10; dufour_angry += 150; unionist_relation -= 20; ddp_relation -= 20; gold_relation -= 20; lvp_relation -= 20; ddp_cohesion -= 5; ddp_right += 6; gold_right += 10; lvp_right += 10
face-image: img/reichsbanner_2.jpg
max-visits: 1
go-to: campaigning_thalmann

Closer ties between the the Banners and the <span style="color: #700000;">**RFB**</span> are established, protecting local party officials from political violence.

@media_communist
title: Use our radio stations to broadcast in favor of [+ communist_candidate_1932 +].
subtitle: This may help in overcoming their antagonism against <span style="color: #700000;">Communists</span>. -1 resource
choose-if: radio >= 2 and resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if radio < 2: We haven't sufficiently built up our radio infrastructure yet. ?] [? if resources < 1: Not enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 1; media_communist_seen = 1; burgher_marcher += (radio + commercialized_media); guild_marcher += (radio + commercialized_media); commons_marcher += (campaign_media + radio - 2); disfavored_marcher += (campaign_media + radio); burgher_collectivist += 3; socialism += 3; nationalism -= 3
face-image: img/poster_0.jpg
max-visits: 1
go-to: campaigning_thalmann

Let's face it, the middle class is never going to support someone like [+ communist_candidate_1932 +], no matter how hard we try. However, we do manage to convince some of our own in the <span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> white-collar unions to come around.

@united_left
title: We persuade the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> to let us take a more active role in their campaign efforts.
subtitle: They have been putting themselves at the forefront. -1 resources
choose-if: (collectivist_relation >= 70 or (collectivist_relation >= 55 and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators")) and resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if (collectivist_relation < 70 or (collectivist_relation < 55 and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators")): Our relations aren't good enough. ?] [? if resources < 2: Not enough resources. (need 2) ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 1; marcher_glaze_thalmann = 1; commons_marcher += 3; commons_collectivist += 3; commons_royalist -= 3; disfavored_marcher += 3; disfavored_collectivist += 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; unionist_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 5; gold_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 5; gold_right += 4; ddp_right += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 2; lvp_right += 4; burgher_collectivist = 1
face-image: img/kpd_poster.jpg
max-visits: 1
go-to: campaigning_thalmann

For some reason, the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> aren't particularly grateful for our endorsement of [+ communist_candidate_1932 +]; perhaps it's due to orders from Moscow. Anyhow, we have managed to convince their leadership to allow us to participate together in joint rallies and other efforts.

@campaigning_hindenburg_op
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.industrial_total_backing) {
    Q.dufour_funds += Q.industrial_ddp_backing;
    Q.dufour_funds += Q.industrial_lvp_backing;
    Q.dufour_funds += Q.industrial_gold_backing;
    Q.dufour_funds += Q.industrial_traditionalist_backing;
    Q.dufour_funds += ((100 - Q.royalist_votes) / 25);
    if (Q.marcher_in_government) Q.dufour_funds += ((100 - Q.collectivist_votes) / 10);
}
Q.dufour_funds_old = Q.dufour_funds;
!}
view-if: not marcher_support_reactionary
go-to: embezzlement_options_op

The finances of the DuFour campaign are in disarray. Influential industrialists and business leaders are withholding significant donations due to his perceived betrayal of the Right. A lingering debt of five million Gold from his 1925 campaign remains unpaid, while additional funds are needed to cover organizational costs. [? if dufour_funds < 5: Efforts to raise money from the parties backing DuFour’s reelection are further complicated by their own financial struggles. Many have already depleted their resources and are carefully preserving what little remains for the upcoming state elections at the end of April. ?][? if dufour_funds >= 5: Fundraising efforts are further hindered by the parties backing DuFour’s reelection, as they prefer to reserve their funds for the upcoming state elections in late April, believing his victory is already assured. ?]

@embezzlement_options_op

- @embezzle_op
- @embezzle_op_2
- @bourgeois_campaign_op: The funding situation is solved.

@embezzle_op
title: Gunther Gereke has miraculously presented millions of Gold from an unknown source.
view-if: bruning_time
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: dufour_funds += 3; burgher_kvp += 2; guild_kvp += 2; landed_kvp += 4; burgher_traditionalist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_traditionalist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; landed_traditionalist += 4 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; landed_other += 4 if not kvp_formed; landed_royalist -= 4 if landed_royalist_normalized >= 35; pro_republic += 3; embezzle_1_op = 1
go-to: embezzlement_options_op

Gunther Gereke, [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>?] member responsible for raising funds for the DuFour campaign, has managed to secure and disburse seven million marks to the campaign—though some of these funds have been diverted to his own party. The volume of private and corporate donations alone would have been insufficient to cover the campaign's expenses, making it evident that state financing, particularly from the Commonwealth Army, played a role.

@embezzle_op_2
title: Gunther Gereke has miraculously presented millions of Gold from an unknown source.
view-if: not bruning_time
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: dufour_funds += 1
go-to: embezzlement_options_op

Gunther Gereke, [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span>?] member responsible for raising funds for the DuFour campaign, has managed to secure and disburse two million marks to the campaign—though some of these funds have been diverted to his own party. The volume of private and corporate donations alone would have been insufficient to cover the campaign's expenses, so we suspect the million or so marks that suddenly materialized was provided by Staal from the Commonwealth Army’s secret funds.

@bourgeois_campaign_op
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.dufour_funds >= 5 && !Q.industrial_dufour) {
    Q.burgher_kvp += Q.dufour_funds / 2;
    Q.guild_kvp += Q.dufour_funds / 2;
    Q.landed_kvp += Q.dufour_funds / 2;
    if (Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") {
        Q.burgher_traditionalist += Q.dufour_funds / 2;
        Q.guild_traditionalist += Q.dufour_funds / 2;
        Q.landed_traditionalist += Q.dufour_funds / 3;
    }
    Q.burgher_other += Q.dufour_funds / 3;
    Q.guild_other += Q.dufour_funds / 3;
    Q.landed_other += Q.dufour_funds / 3;
    Q.burgher_gold += Q.dufour_funds / 3;
    Q.guild_gold += Q.dufour_funds / 3;
    Q.landed_gold += Q.dufour_funds / 4;
    Q.burgher_lvp += Q.dufour_funds / 2;
    Q.guild_lvp += Q.dufour_funds / 2;
    Q.landed_lvp += Q.dufour_funds / 4;
}
Q.industrial_dufour = 1;

Q.dufour_unity = 10;
if (Q.dufour_angry_bruning >= 75) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.gold_defect) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.cnblp_defect) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.second_bruning_cabinet_seen) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.royalist_votes >= 25) Q.dufour_unity -= 1;
if (Q.marcher_support_reactionary) Q.dufour_unity -= 3;
if (Q.marcher_campaign || Q.marcher_support_thalmann || Q.collectivist_support_marcher) Q.dufour_unity += 3;
!}
view-if: dufour_funds > dufour_funds_old
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu_op

The United DuFour Committees have set to work improving the perception of moderate right-wing Commonwealth voters toward President DuFour, whose reputation as the Hero of Tannenberg has been tarnished by his support for the hated Unity system. Despite this, the <span class="tooltip-text" title="Following DuFour's overseeing of the Commonwealth's crushing victory at Tannenberg in the Great War, DuFour has become the center of a massive personality cult, lauded as the living ideal of Commonwealth masculinity and patriotism. He is the embodiment of the best virtues of Heartland tradition.">DuFour Mythos</span> remains intact[? if royalist_candidate_1932 == "Gallax":, and may be the only thing that rivals Gallax's charisma?].

It's their turn to campaign.

DuFour camp unity level: [+ dufour_unity : dufour_unity +]

@bourgeois_campaign_menu_op
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.unionist_support_marcher != 1) Q.religion_available = 1;
!}

- @eckener_op
- @industrial_op
- @religion_op
- @westarp_op
- @organizational_endorsements_op

@eckener_op
title: Famed Zeppelin Captain Hugo Eckhart is recruited for the campaign.
subtitle: Being a stanch support of the President, he will utilize the *Graf Zeppelin* for the campaign.
on-arrival: eckener_used = 1
max-visits: 1
go-to: eckener_2_op if dufour_unity >= 8; eckener_3_op if dufour_unity < 8

@eckener_2_op
on-arrival: dufour_support += 2
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu_op

In an attempt to rival the <span class="tooltip-text" title="good mod">dynamism</span> of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> campaign, which has utilized aircraft to quickly transport high-profile <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> leaders to deliver up to four speeches per day, Hugo Eckhart has been convinced to take flight across the Commonwealth to drum up popular support for DuFour. 

@eckener_3_op
on-arrival: disfavored_royalist += 6; disfavored_collectivist -= 3; disfavored_marcher -= 3
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu_op

In an attempt to rival the dynamism of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> campaign, the DuFour campaign initially tried to convince Graf Zeppelin pilot Hugo Eckhart to fly across the Commonwealth in support of DuFour. However, with Eckhart already scheduled for a flight to South America, the campaign had to pivot to an alternative approach. They opted to rent airplanes to drop twenty million leaflets over the Commonwealth population. However, this isn't enough to counteract the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> style of campaigning.

@industrial_op
title: Carl Duisberg of IG Farben will attempt to gain support of key industrialists.
subtitle: DuFour has lost the favor of many of his former backers, maybe they can be convinced again?
on-arrival: industry_used = 1
max-visits: 1
go-to: industrial_2_op if dufour_unity >= 5; industrial_3_op if dufour_unity < 5

Carl Duisberg, the chairman of the United DuFour Committees have largely been unsuccessful in convincing big business leaders to sign the petition for DuFour's reelection, but perhaps the gravity of this race would help convince them?

@industrial_2_op
on-arrival: dufour_support += 2
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu_op

Duisberg, being the former chairman of the National Federation of Commonwealth Industry (RDI) and one of the more moderate members, has been successful in soliciting donations from many business leaders who had reservations about backing DuFour again. The radical revolutionary and socialistic policies of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> have greatly discouraged them from donating to [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]. It now looks like the DuFour campaign finally has the resources to properly establish a campaign infrastructure that can rival Goebbels' efforts and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>.

@industrial_3_op
on-arrival: guild_royalist += 4; guild_kvp -= 2; guild_traditionalist -= 2 if industrial_traditionalist_backing >= 2 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_other -= 4; landed_royalist += 2
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu_op

Despite the antipathy the industrialists have toward [? if not gallax_deported: Gallax and the ?]<span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> due to their crypto-<span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> policies, a large part of them are firmly opposed to DuFour, and will withhold their donations. The DuFour campaign is beginning to heavily fall behind the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> in more rural areas, primarily due to the lack of resources.

@religion_op
title: The Catholic Church and Lutheran Church have long held political neutrality, perhaps that will change?
view-if: unionist_support_marcher != 1
on-arrival: religion_used = 1; faithful_unionist += 4 if faithful_unionist_normalized < 50; faithful_royalist -= 4 if faithful_unionist_normalized < 50 and faithful_royalist_normalized >= 8
max-visits: 1
go-to: religion_2_op if dufour_unity >= 3; religion_3_op if dufour_unity < 3

Prominent leaders of the Lutheran Church have endorsed President DuFour, arguing that despite their historical political neutrality, his reelection is a pressing necessity. Meanwhile, the Catholic Church is even more united in support of DuFour than it was for Wilhelm Marx in 1925. Catholic leaders, historically skeptical of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazism</span>, have actively discouraged their members from joining <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> paramilitary organizations. This, combined with the strong support of Catholic-affiliated trade unions, will prove enormously significant in rallying a skeptical Catholic population behind a candidate whom most instinctively associate with Lutheran orthodoxy and Heartland authoritarianism.

@religion_2_op
on-arrival: dufour_support += 1
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu_op

Despite strong opposition from state and local Protestant church organizations—many of whose members sympathize with [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +] and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>—they have taken a public stand and will be campaigning in favor of DuFour, even amid growing calls for them to withdraw their endorsements.

@religion_3_op
on-arrival: burgher_royalist += 2; guild_royalist += 2; landed_royalist += 2; burgher_kvp -= 2; guild_kvp -= 2; landed_kvp -= 2; burgher_traditionalist -= 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_traditionalist -= 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; landed_traditionalist -= 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; burgher_other -= 2 if not kvp_formed; guild_other -= 2 if not kvp_formed; landed_other -= 2 if not kvp_formed
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu_op

Unfortunately for the DuFour campaign, the pro-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> sentiment within state and local churches has prevented church leaders from taking a public stand for DuFour. Many devout Protestants will now be voting for [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +] as a result, as the church now claims that intervening in a presidential election would be against its nature.

@westarp_op
title: Westmore, one of DuFour's close friends, will attempt to rally conservative forces for DuFour.
on-arrival: westarp_used = 1; dufour_support += 1
view-if: not marcher_campaign_1932
max-visits: 1
go-to: bourgeois_campaign_menu_op

Of course, the main goal of the United DuFour Committees is to dispel the notion that DuFour is supported by the <span style="color: #000000;">Black</span>-<span style="color: #c00000;">Red</span> parties. To this end, Westmore has sent a letter to 750 conservative elites who supported DuFour's election in 1925, with 500 reaffirming their support of DuFour today. [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": He has also played a key role in rallying the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> around his candidacy. ?]

@organizational_endorsements_op
title: What about the endorsements of the non-partisan organizations?
subtitle: Influential groups such as the RLB, DHV, and the Pan-Germans, have been growing a rift between themselves and DuFour.
view-if: eckener_used and industry_used and (religion_used or not religion_available) and nd (westarp_used or marcher_candidate_1932)
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.dufour_support) {
    Q.burgher_kvp += Q.dufour_support;
    Q.guild_kvp += Q.dufour_support; 
    Q.landed_kvp += Q.dufour_support;
    if (Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") {
        Q.burgher_traditionalist += Q.dufour_support;
        Q.guild_traditionalist += Q.dufour_support;
        Q.landed_traditionalist += Q.dufour_support;
    }
    Q.burgher_ddp += Q.dufour_support / 3; 
    Q.guild_ddp += Q.dufour_support / 3;
    Q.burgher_other += Q.dufour_support / 1.5;
    Q.guild_other += Q.dufour_support / 1.5;
    Q.burgher_gold += Q.dufour_support / 3;
    Q.guild_gold += Q.dufour_support / 3;
    Q.landed_other += Q.dufour_support / 1.5;
    Q.pro_republic += Q.dufour_support; 
    if (!Q.kvp_formed && Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Radical") Q.landed_other += Q.dufour_support;
    Q.burgher_royalist -= (Q.dufour_support*Q.royalist_votes) / 50;
    Q.old_royalist -= (Q.dufour_support*Q.royalist_votes) / 50;
    Q.landed_royalist -= (Q.dufour_support*Q.royalist_votes) / 50;
}
if (Q.rlb_royalist) {
    Q.rlb_dufour = 0;
    Q.landed_royalist += Q.landed_other*0.1;
    Q.landed_other *= 0.9;
    Q.landed_traditionalist *= 0.9;
} else if (!Q.rlb_royalist) {
    Q.rlb_dufour = 1;
    Q.landed_other += 4;
    if (Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") {
        Q.landed_traditionalist += 2;
    } else {
        Q.landed_kvp += 2;
    }
}
!}

National Rural League (RLB) - [? if rlb_dufour: <span style="color: #808080;">**[+ reactionary_candidate_1932_disp +]**</span> ?][? if not rlb_dufour: <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**[+ royalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>[? if traditionalist_candidate_1932:&nbsp;or <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**[+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +]**</span>?] ?]

